                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8fc81da4-86b8-3f2e-a871-518bfb38a759",
                        "entry_id": "c72592b5-566b-3cd3-90f1-366515437450",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the open sea, especially as a place to fish"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "Shetland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "988179d1-2971-4210-97ad-2dbe3544a01e",
                                "sense_id": "8fc81da4-86b8-3f2e-a871-518bfb38a759",
                                "text": "The banks to which they repair for the haaf fishing, are often many miles distant from the station where the fish is dried; so that they are always twenty or thirty hours absent, frequently longer; and under unfavourable circumstances of wind and tide, they remain at sea, with a very small stock of provisions, and in a boat of a construction which seems extremely slender, for two or three days, and are sometimes heard of no more."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b4175a3-7c47-40ff-ab32-f5905eabb77f",
                                "sense_id": "8fc81da4-86b8-3f2e-a871-518bfb38a759",
                                "text": "The haaf-boat was as well maintained as any vessel in the islands; her master had a reputation for thoroughness, for all he was barely twenty years of age."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa60c957-e603-3629-9432-9ac0788d1191",
                        "entry_id": "c72592b5-566b-3cd3-90f1-366515437450",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the practice of sea fishing for such as cod, ling and tusk"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Shetland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9c26f9e-526f-4877-9537-66b208be59f1",
                                "sense_id": "fa60c957-e603-3629-9432-9ac0788d1191",
                                "text": "Although men concentrated at the main haaf stations during the summer fishing season, they reverted to their homes in crofting townships for the remainder of the year."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
